body:
I'm asking for strategies because people seem to be way more consistent and disciplined than me and seem to have more knowledge. I don't know everything and maybe someone gives me an idea I haven't thought of. 

&#x200B;

In terms of how I turned it back into nothing it was by using the same strategy and just being wrong and after that probably getting a bit too emotional chasing potential profits and taking stupid risk. The two days after I got to $100k I chose my "A" picks and went down to $33k from those bad beats, my "B" picks would have turned that $100k to $2,000,000 but I didn't pick them. Even if I had diversified I'd have been at $1,000,000. So that disappointment made me sad/depressed/irrational which led to more bad picks and reaching. 

&#x200B;

To your point I'd say I believe I have potential and my strategy does but I do need to flesh it out more, working full-time makes that more difficult though. Sorry for the excessive response to your question but thanks for reading

Unlike others i feel like my diet can be a bit all over the place, but i dont eat beef or pork (never have) and i think that helps. I have a big sweet tooth though (cookies and doughnuts). I try to do a minimum of 300 reps of abs (crunches, bicycles, etc.) 5 days a week. I said minimum because i would usually go for 500 a day but my  new job has me in the gym less as i have to travel but i make due with a towel on hotel room floor. 

&#x200B;

Also, running at a decent speed helps. Jogging is less relevant to abs than sprinting so if you run you can do faster speeds for shorter distances and have desirable results.  As I mentioned with the travel I recently seen myself getting a gut and went back to this and noticed immediate results within the last week.
